        "id": 4069542
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-17T22:46:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems fishy to me.\n\nSo url match here filters out urls and we get some hashcode mapping and then we do another filter during PushOne without url match (its null) which gives different mapping and we might always loose some refs.....",
      "revId": "d5e70dd7e0e06fdc86364c9b72459f81fa02a2f4",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55f46c77_4eb63f74",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/googlesource/gerrit/plugins/replication/ReplicationQueue.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 4651293
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T04:29:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "urlMatch is only ever set by scheduleFullSync, whose ALL_REFS marker is never hashed, so real ref names always arrive with urlMatch null.\npush-time ownership uses the full URL list deliberately so every node derives the same mapping, and replication start --url X then syncs exactly the refs X owns.",
      "parentUuid": "987d7c5e_215784df",
      "revId": "d5e70dd7e0e06fdc86364c9b72459f81fa02a2f4",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "910f851f_deeb2464",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/googlesource/gerrit/plugins/replication/ReplicationQueue.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 4069542
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T07:37:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So when we specify a start --all with url match, it still ends up pushing to all the urls (and hence all refs) or are we pushing only to that URL and the refs it owns ?\n\nBoth of them seem wrong to me.",
      "parentUuid": "55f46c77_4eb63f74",
      "revId": "d5e70dd7e0e06fdc86364c9b72459f81fa02a2f4",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59697c49_b0214b35",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/googlesource/gerrit/plugins/replication/ReplicationQueue.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 4665459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-19T01:31:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With `replication start all --url url1`, it looks like only the shard of refs owned by url1 will be pushed (@bhoomikas, correct me if I am wrong). The rest are skipped, which feels counter-intuitive to me. Should we show a warning or disallow passing a url via --url if it belongs to a refSharded remote? Additionally, now that the start command has a --ref option, won\u0027t its interaction with --url and refSharded have a similar implication?\n\nAdmins should probably be encouraged (by updating the docs?) to use `replication start` with --remote instead of --url when refSharded is in play.",
      "parentUuid": "910f851f_deeb2464",
      "revId": "d5e70dd7e0e06fdc86364c9b72459f81fa02a2f4",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e075335_105e3399",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/googlesource/gerrit/plugins/replication/ReplicationQueue.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-19T16:19:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To me, the desired behavior is to only push to the refs which cover the specified url. If the url matches more than one host, it should push to the refs which shard to those hosts only. This feels consistent, and correct.  It also is useful, it allows a subset of the refs to be pushed to reduce load. It avoids double pushing the same refs at the same time as a refupdate push, which is the intent of this strategy. I all the refs need to be pushed, then the admin can specify the remote instead.",
      "parentUuid": "59697c49_b0214b35",
      "revId": "d5e70dd7e0e06fdc86364c9b72459f81fa02a2f4",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
