      "author": {
        "id": 4651293
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-20T16:28:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is what the code now does, and for any subset of refs rather than only a full sync: placement is computed over all configured URLs and `--url` only narrows which of them are pushed to, so a targeted URL gets the refs it owns instead of every ref re-hashed onto it. `--ref` does not exist on `stable-3.11`, but `--ref` R `--url X` will follow the same rule when this merges forward. Documented, with `--remote` for syncing every `ref`.",
      "parentUuid": "8e075335_105e3399",
      "revId": "d5e70dd7e0e06fdc86364c9b72459f81fa02a2f4",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
